window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-8486fe00c240100d"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"use-the-codex-security-workbench\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-security\">使用 Codex Security 工作台</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用 Security 工作台启动扫描、审阅已保存的发现项，并查看代码库的扫描历史。每次扫描都在一个 Codex 任务中运行，你可以打开该任务查看运行情况。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，打开 ChatGPT 下拉菜单并选择 <strong>Codex</strong>。安装并启用 <a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security 插件</a>，然后在侧边栏中选择 <strong>Security（安全）</strong>。</p> <p>如果没有看到 <strong>Security（安全）</strong>，请确认当前选中的是 <strong>Codex</strong>，并且插件已安装且启用。必要时更新桌面应用和插件，并确认工作区管理员是否允许使用该插件。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">启动扫描</h2> <p>为获得较好的扫描质量，请使用 <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code>，并选择 <code>xhigh</code> 推理强度。</p> <ol> <li>打开 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>并选择 <strong>+ Scan（新建扫描）</strong>。</li> <li>选择一个已有代码库，或选择其他文件夹。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Codebase（代码库）</strong>扫描代码库，或选择 <strong>Changes（更改）</strong>审查基于 Git 的更改。</li> <li>设置扫描范围。对于 <strong>Codebase（代码库）</strong>，选择整个代码库或某个文件夹。开启 <strong>Deep scan（深度扫描）</strong>，对所选代码库进行多轮审查。对于 <strong>Changes（更改）</strong>，选择未提交的更改、某个提交或一个修订版本范围。更改扫描不支持深度扫描。</li> <li>选择模型和推理强度。使用 <strong>Additional context（补充上下文）</strong>提供威胁模型或部署环境的细节。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Start scan（开始扫描）</strong>。</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: Codex Security 工作台显示新建代码库扫描的设置界面</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 在 Security 工作台中选择代码库并配置扫描。 </figcaption> <p>有关各类扫描的详细说明，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">运行安全扫描</a>、<a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">运行深度安全扫描</a>或<a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">审查代码更改中的安全问题</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"follow-scan-progress\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">跟踪扫描进度</h2> <p>扫描页面会显示当前阶段以及插件报告的进度。</p> <p>选择 <strong>View activity（查看活动）</strong>可打开运行扫描的 Codex 任务。你可以离开工作台，之后再返回 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>，已保存的扫描不会丢失。若要停止任务，请打开扫描并选择 <strong>Stop scan（停止扫描）</strong>。</p> <p>扫描完成后，打开结果，检查目标、修订版本、发现项、覆盖范围和可用的报告文件。</p> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: 已完成的 Codex Security 扫描，显示发现项、扫描覆盖范围和报告文件</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 扫描完成后，审阅发现项、严重性、扫描覆盖范围和生成的文件。 </figcaption> <p><a id=\"review-findings-across-scans\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">跨扫描审阅发现项</h2> <p>打开 <strong>Findings（发现项）</strong>，查看不同代码库和扫描中保存的发现项。搜索或筛选列表，然后选择一条发现项，审阅其摘要、源代码证据、验证情况和影响。</p> <p>查看发现项详细信息时使用 <strong>Summary（摘要）</strong>；需要生成、审阅、应用或验证修复时使用 <strong>Patch（补丁）</strong>。有关修复流程，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">修复并验证安全发现项</a>。</p> <p><strong>Findings（发现项）</strong>标签页显示已保存的 Codex Security 扫描中的发现项。导入的工单和其他既有安全问题仍属于单独的<a href=\"#/article/a-3623d131a0f26273\">待办问题分流流程</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-repository-history\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">查看代码库历史</h2> <p>打开 <strong>Repositories（代码库）</strong>，浏览可用的代码库和文件夹。选择一个代码库，可查看其扫描历史、最近扫描的修订版本和未解决的发现项。在代码库详情中，你可以打开以前的扫描，或查看与该代码库相关的发现项。</p> <p>如果代码库尚无扫描记录，可以从代码库详情启动扫描，或在工作台中选择 <strong>+ Scan（新建扫描）</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-scan-from-a-conversation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">从对话启动扫描</h2> <p>你也可以在普通对话中要求 Codex 运行已安装的 Codex Security 插件。使用共享插件工作台的扫描会显示在 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>中，你可以返回 Security 工作台继续查看其进度和结果。</p> <p>有关基于终端的扫描和自动化，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">Codex Security CLI 快速入门</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"use-the-codex-security-workbench\">Use the Codex Security workbench</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use the Security workbench to start scans, review saved findings, and inspect a repository's scan history. Each scan runs in a Codex task you can open to inspect its activity.</p> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, open the ChatGPT dropdown and select <strong>Codex</strong>. Install and enable the <a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security plugin</a>, then select <strong>Security</strong> in the sidebar.</p> <p>If <strong>Security</strong> doesn't appear, confirm that <strong>Codex</strong> is selected and the plugin is installed and enabled. Update the desktop app and plugin if needed, and check whether your workspace administrator allows the plugin.</p> <h2 id=\"start-a-scan\">Start a scan</h2> <p>For the best scan quality, use <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code> with <code>xhigh</code> reasoning effort.</p> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Scans</strong> and select <strong>+ Scan</strong>.</li> <li>Select an existing repository or choose another folder.</li> <li>Choose <strong>Codebase</strong> to scan a repository or <strong>Changes</strong> to review a Git-backed change.</li> <li>Set the scope. For <strong>Codebase</strong>, choose the entire repository or a folder. Turn on <strong>Deep scan</strong> for repeated review of the selected codebase. For <strong>Changes</strong>, choose uncommitted changes, a commit, or a revision range. Deep scans aren't available for changes.</li> <li>Choose a model and reasoning effort. Use <strong>Additional context</strong> for threat-model or deployment details.</li> <li>Select <strong>Start scan</strong>.</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Codex Security workbench showing the setup for a new repository scan</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Choose a repository and configure a scan in the Security workbench. </figcaption> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">Run a security scan</a>, <a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">Run a deep security scan</a>, or <a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">Review code changes for security</a> for details about each scan type.</p> <h2 id=\"follow-scan-progress\">Follow scan progress</h2> <p>The scan page shows the current phase and any progress the plugin reports.</p> <p>Select <strong>View activity</strong> to open the Codex task that runs the scan. You can leave the workbench and return to <strong>Scans</strong> without losing a saved scan. To stop work, open the scan and select <strong>Stop scan</strong>.</p> <p>When the scan completes, open its results to review the target, revision, findings, coverage, and available report artifacts.</p> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Completed Codex Security scan showing findings, scan coverage, and report artifacts</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Review findings, severity, scan coverage, and artifacts after a scan completes. </figcaption> <h2 id=\"review-findings-across-scans\">Review findings across scans</h2> <p>Open <strong>Findings</strong> to inspect saved findings across repositories and scans. Search or filter the list, then select a finding to review its summary, source evidence, validation, and impact.</p> <p>Use <strong>Summary</strong> for the finding details and <strong>Patch</strong> when you want to generate, review, apply, or verify a fix. See <a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">Fix and verify security findings</a> for the remediation workflow.</p> <p>The <strong>Findings</strong> tab shows findings from saved Codex Security scans. Imported tickets and other existing security issues remain part of the separate <a href=\"#/article/a-3623d131a0f26273\">backlog triage workflow</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"inspect-repository-history\">Inspect repository history</h2> <p>Open <strong>Repositories</strong> to browse available repositories and folders. Select a repository to inspect its scan history, latest scanned revision, and open findings. From repository details, open a previous scan or view the findings associated with that repository.</p> <p>If a repository has no scans, start a scan from its details or select <strong>+ Scan</strong> in the workbench.</p> <h2 id=\"start-a-scan-from-a-conversation\">Start a scan from a conversation</h2> <p>You can also ask Codex to run the installed Codex Security plugin in a regular conversation. Scans that use the shared plugin workbench appear in <strong>Scans</strong>, so you can return to their progress and results from the Security workbench.</p> <p>For terminal-based scans and automation, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">Codex Security CLI quickstart</a>.</p>"};
